comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T07:58:00.774Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: all-status searches for the exact GH-733 title, run identifier, Windows Node 24, and the three failing spec names found no live canonical owner. Closed pm-3x8w4m and pm-lt6n are precedent for earlier cross-platform regressions; open pm-tgq6 is a distinct stale-cleanup flake. This item owns only run 30191427127 / GH-733."
  "2026-07-26T08:01:07.778Z","harness:codex","Evidence: the three GH-733 regression specs pass 27/27 after switching author-source expectations to native separators, building recovery roots with node:path, and injecting the inaccessible-history errno seam directly instead of relying on chmod or parent-path behavior. Repo-wide lint also passes: ESLint, zero jscpd clones, 100% source/export/member docstrings, package boundary, token budget, SDK snapshot, SDK import-cost, and CLI transport gates. Exact Windows Node 24 proof remains pending on the pushed PR head, so this item stays in progress and claimed."
  "2026-07-26T08:02:14.581Z","harness:codex","PR evidence: GH-733 fixes are published in PR #734 head 185693b9. The item remains in progress and claimed until the exact Windows Node 24 check is terminal and green."
  "2026-07-26T08:07:48.330Z","harness:codex","Exact-host evidence: PR #734 head 9be76ad6 passed the required Windows regression (Node 24) job in 2m07s, plus all four coverage shards, 100% aggregate coverage, static/typecheck/compat/smoke, macOS and Ubuntu runtime smokes, CodeQL, Semgrep, Trivy, TruffleHog, DeepScan, CodeFactor, docs, ShellCheck, PSScriptAnalyzer, actionlint, and Codecov patch coverage. The prior GH-733 false negatives are eliminated on the authoritative platform."
  "2026-07-26T08:29:32.589Z","harness:codex","Final-head evidence: PR #734 e2453835 repeated the Windows Node 24 regression, four coverage shards, 100% aggregate coverage, static/typecheck/compat/smoke, security, hosted analysis, and Codecov gates successfully."
